# ResumeModeCancelledQueue — re-enqueue every captured order +
# instant-action from the AGV's mode-cancelled buffer at the FRONT
# of the live queue (preserves original FMS-intended ordering).
# Service half of Task #24.
#
# **When to call**: typically on the AUTOMATIC return edge of
# `on_mode_changed` (or its equivalent for non-C++ FMS). The
# buffer is populated by the library at every AUTOMATIC →
# non-AUTOMATIC mode transition.
#
# **Ordering**: buffered items go to the FRONT of the live queue.
# Example — buffer captured (orderA, orderB) at leave-AUTOMATIC;
# during AUTOMATIC return, FMS sent orderC; FMS calls resume →
# live queue becomes (orderA, orderB, orderC); AGV processes them
# in that order.
#
# **Validator chain**: re-enqueued items still go through the full
# pre-send / graph / traversability chain at publish time. If an
# AGV moved during MANUAL and the order's first node is no longer
# reachable, that order alone is rejected; the rest still flow.

string manufacturer
string serial_number
---
# Status enum.
#
# SUCCESS              — at least one item was re-enqueued (or
#                        buffer was empty AND empty buffer is OK).
# AGV_NOT_ONBOARDED    — no AGV with this {manufacturer,
#                        serial_number} is currently in the master's
#                        onboard list.
# INVALID_REQUEST      — empty manufacturer or serial_number.
uint8 SUCCESS=0
uint8 AGV_NOT_ONBOARDED=1
uint8 INVALID_REQUEST=2
uint8 status

# Echo of request — async-fanout correlation.
string manufacturer
string serial_number

# Counts of items moved from buffer to the live queue. Both zero is
# valid SUCCESS — buffer was empty (e.g. AGV was never in
# AUTOMATIC, or FMS already called resume / discard).
uint32 orders_resumed
uint32 actions_resumed
